\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Dataset statistics. ArXiv and AAPD use a 64/16/20 split; the other text datasets follow their released partitions; FunCat and GO datasets use the train/validation/test files shipped with the benchmark ARFFs. The \textbf  {Train} column reports train$+$validation, the partition actually optimized in our runs: where a release ships a validation file it is merged back in, and where it does not (the four cross-domain datasets), 20\% of the training file is held out for validation and merged back, so the counts here are the benchmark's training partitions and no test document is ever optimized on.}}{9}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
